# A recursion nothing can see past.
#
# Every way through this body calls the function again, so no trace ever
# reaches a value, and there is nothing for a second trace to be checked
# against. The checker says which function it could not work out and
# what would fix it, rather than looping or guessing.
#
# This program is expected to FAIL type checking. Its `.ast.out` holds
# the error message, not a program's output.

def forever(n):
    forever(n + 1)

print(forever(1))
